Bootstrap: docker
From: ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-cuda

# ============================================================================= #
#    Built from llama.cpp's official CUDA server image, with nothing installed:  #
#    the compute nodes block the user namespaces that a %post section needs     #
#    (Ubuntu 24.04, apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns = 1), so the image    #
#    may only copy files in. The tool is published self-contained, so it needs  #
#    no .NET runtime; the base image has the ICU and OpenSSL libraries it uses. #
#                                                                               #
#    Not pinned: every image build takes the latest llama.cpp. The tool         #
#    records the version in every output file, and resume refuses to mix        #
#    versions, so avoid rebuilding the image in the middle of an experiment.    #
#                                                                               #
#    GPUs: the image carries native code for the RTX 3090 / RTX A4000 (86) and  #
#    portable code that the driver compiles on first use for the GTX 1080 (61), #
#    RTX 2080 Ti / Titan RTX (75) and A100 (80).                                #
# ============================================================================= #

%labels
    Author Márton Gergő
    Version 3.0
    Description Code readability tool with llama.cpp, for the NIPG cluster

%files
    publish /opt/readability

%environment
    # llama-server and its libraries live in /app in the base image.
    export PATH=/app:$PATH
    export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/app:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}
    # Room for the GPU code the driver compiles on first use (kept in ~/.nv between jobs).
    export CUDA_CACHE_MAXSIZE=4294967296

%runscript
    exec /opt/readability/ReadabilityConsoleApp "$@"

%help
    Code readability tool. Run it from the project folder (~/readability) so that its
    output, datasets and checkpoints folders land there:

        apptainer run --nv readabilityconsoleapp.sif help

    On the cluster, use scripts/submit.sh instead of running it directly.
